  "user_scenario": "You are Joyce Gerhardt, 58, a school bus dispatcher who lives in Neenah. You are polite, a bit wary of paperwork, and you want this finished today. At the end of March you went to Riverbend Lakeshore Hospital in Neenah with chest pain and were kept for observation from March 30 to April 1; you paid the 150-dollar copay on Riverbend's portal in May. Later your insurer, Network Health, reviewed the stay and decided it had not been medically necessary. Riverbend appealed, and in July you signed Network Health's form so Riverbend could appeal for you a second time. In August Network Health wrote that the decision was upheld and that you could still ask for an independent external review. You have decided you do not want an external review: you are calling to say so and to have this settled so that you are never billed for the stay.\n\nYou open by saying who you are, Joyce Gerhardt, that you are calling from your home number 9205550243, and why you are calling: Network Health's last letter says you can ask for an outside review of your observation stay, you do not want to ask for one, and you want the stay settled so you never get a bill for it. When the representative asks you to confirm who you are, you give your date of birth, 1968-07-23, and your ZIP code, 54956; if they need one more detail, the medical record number on Riverbend's letters is RB22803517. If they ask about your insurance, it is Network Health through your employer, member ID NH227049318, group 220917.\n\nYou will not request the external review, and you are not going to ask Network Health for anything else either; if the representative asks, that is your answer, said simply. If they explain that Riverbend has some things of its own to settle on the claim first, or ask whether they may go ahead with what they need to do, you tell them that is fine and to go ahead. You do not know any dollar figures beyond your copay and you do not question the ones you are given.\n\nWhen the representative hands the step for recording your decision over to you and tells you the claim reference and the amount to enter, you enter exactly what they told you and read the confirmation back to them. Once your decision is recorded you thank them and end the call.",
